 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all (the initial call and 4 retries).
+The pauses before retries are 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds. A successful attempt returns the charge id immediately; if all
+5 attempts time out, the final `GatewayTimeout` is raised. The pauses add up to 20 seconds to the member's wait on
+the confirmation page, in addition to the time spent waiting for the gateway.
+
+Previously, 3 attempts ran back to back within a second. During the gateway's Friday peak, 17:00 to 19:00, all
+3 could hit the same slowdown: 58 confirmed pantry orders went uncharged and a volunteer captured them by hand the
+next morning. Replaying those timeouts in the sandbox with the new schedule would have recovered 57 of the 58.
+The maintainer accepted the longer confirmation wait to reduce manual captures; switching gateways was ruled out
+because the contract runs to December 2026. This evidence and choice are recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
